# Team blog

Week 1
For our first group meeting, we got to know each other and established each members’ skills.
We found that we naturally had a good balance of frontend, backend, technical management and project
management skills between us. We set up a GitHub page and talked through some initial project ideas.

Next steps were:
- Set deadline of Monday week 2 to decide on final idea for software project and agreed to continue discussions online (through GitHub discussion).
- Agreed weekly meetings on Mondays online at 4.15pm, and to keep these going even if they were just very quick as a way of touching base

Week 2
We meet online and  discussed all the options that had been put forward in our GitHub discussion, we considered them in turn in terms of a range of considerations including:
-the ability to deliver a prototype in the timescale, 
-scalability,
-interests and skills within the team.

Alternatives that were discussed were blog-engine, an accessibility checker, personal language translator for video language learning
We agreed on the Blog Engine idea in the end as it seemed to have the best potential to be scalable and was a challenging and innovative idea
Mei as Technical Lead and initiator of this idea agreed to flesh out an initial Specification Document that we would all work on collaboratoratively on GitHb.

